<%# A single headline figure with its label.

    Stripe reading: the number is the content, so it gets the size and weight and
    the label stays quiet above it. Figures use tabular-nums so a row of stats
    lines up rather than jittering.

    Built with tag.div rather than a literal element because the optional
    data-testid has to be omitted entirely when absent - interpolating it into the
    markup produced an unquoted attribute that selectors could not match.

    Locals:
      label  - what the figure is
      value  - the figure, already formatted
      icon      - optional Lucide name, as a 32px tile on the label's line
      icon_tone - tone for that tile (:neutral default)
      hint      - optional supporting line
      change    - optional comparison line, already formatted
      change_up - true for a gain, false for a loss; sets the arrow and the colour
      testid - optional data-testid, for tests targeting a specific stat %>
<%# .tw-card, not its own rounded-xl / shadow-xs surface. This was a fourth card treatment: the
    portfolio page put three of these beside a .tw-card chart, a .tw-card summary and a
    hand-rolled h-[150px] panel, so four radii and three shadows shared one screen.

    `surface: false` renders the figure with no card of its own, for a group of them **inside** one card.
    A strip of separate cards is right where the figures are the page's summary and stand alone - the
    portfolio does that - and wrong where they are one section among several: four cards for four
    figures on `classrooms#show` took that page from two surfaces to six, which is the card-soup shape
    its own test forbids. One component either way, because the alternative is a second way to render a
    figure and this document has watched that happen four times. %>
<% surface = local_assigns.fetch(:surface, true) %>
<%= tag.div class: (surface ? "tw-card p-5" : ""),
            data: { testid: local_assigns[:testid] } do %>
  <%# A leading icon goes on the label's line, at the 32px size - the same place and size as the
      home page's balance card and _card's header. best_month used to hang its tile off the right
      in an items-start justify-between row, so two cards sitting side by side in one grid row
      mirrored each other. design.md: the icon belongs on the title's line, and 32px is the size
      for a tile next to a 14px label; 36px is for a tile on its own line above a figure, which is
      what the admin dashboard does. %>
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
    <% if local_assigns[:icon].present? %>
      <%= render "components/ui/icon_tile",
                 icon: icon, tone: local_assigns.fetch(:icon_tone, :neutral), compact: true %>
    <% end %>
    <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-600"><%= label %></p>
  </div>
  <%# 8px under a tile row, 4px under a bare label. The seam is measured from whatever is above it:
      a 32px tile row needs more air than a 20px line of text, and the home page's balance card
      already used mt-2 for exactly this. Three values were in play for one seam - 4px here, 8px on
      home, 12px in money_at_work. %>
  <p class="<%= local_assigns[:icon].present? ? 'mt-2' : 'mt-1' %> text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 tabular-nums"><%= value %></p>
  <%# A comparison line, when the figure has something to compare against. The sign and the arrow
      carry the direction as well as the colour, so a loss does not depend on being able to tell
      green from red. green-700/red-700 clear AA where 600 does not. %>
  <% if local_assigns[:change].present? %>
    <p class="mt-1 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-medium <%= local_assigns[:change_up] ? 'text-green-700' : 'text-red-700' %>">
      <%= lucide_icon(local_assigns[:change_up] ? "trending-up" : "trending-down", class: "size-3.5 shrink-0") %>
      <%= change %>
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <% if local_assigns[:hint].present? %>
    <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500"><%= hint %></p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
